meta {
  name: Add Custom Method Technique
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/incidents/custom-technique
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 2
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "technique_name": "Modified basket hold with verbal de-poiuygf"
  }
}

docs {
  # Add Custom Method/Technique
  
  Adds a custom method/technique for physical interventions that can be reused for future incidents.
  This is useful when the standard options (Baskethold, Two-arm hold, etc.) don't match the technique used.
  
  ## Request Body:
  ```json
  {
    "technique_name": "Custom technique name"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response:
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Custom technique added successfully",
    "data": {
      "value": "Custom technique name",
      "label": "Custom technique name",
      "custom": true,
      "house_id": 4,
      "client_id": 1
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Use Case:
  1. User selects "Other" from the method/technique dropdown
  2. User enters custom technique in the text field
  3. Optionally, call this endpoint to save the custom technique for future use
  4. The technique will appear in the dropdown for subsequent incidents
  
  ## Future Enhancement:
  Once saved, custom techniques will be included in the "Get Method Technique Options" endpoint response.
}
